Backport from mainline Linux ("I2C & I3C" row of the CIX upstream wiki; the
Sky1 I2C ports use the Cadence I2C driver, cdns,i2c-r1p14):
f612925f989 "i2c: cadence: Add shutdown handler".

On reboot/kexec an I2C transfer that is in flight (or started by a late
shutdown path) could leave the controller with HOLD set, interrupts enabled
and data in the FIFO, so the next kernel or the firmware found the bus busy
and some I2C devices (USB-C PD controller, HDMI/DP helpers, sensors) did not
answer after a warm reboot. The controller is now marked suspended (new
transfers get -ESHUTDOWN instead of racing with the reboot) and reset.

The board powers off and reboots through PSCI/SCMI, not through an I2C PMIC,
so nothing needs I2C after the controller is shut down.
Not ported: mainline's atomic (polled) transfer support, which needs the
driver's clock handling reworked and has no user on the Orion O6.

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-cadence.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-cadence.c
index 87c42d60e..1c46cc6f0 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-cadence.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,28 @@ static void cdns_i2c_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	clk_disable_unprepare(id->clk);
 }
 
+/**
+ * cdns_i2c_shutdown - Prepare I2C controller for system shutdown
+ * @pdev:	Handle to the platform device structure
+ *
+ * Mark the adapter as suspended and reset the controller to ensure a clean
+ * handoff during system reboot or kexec (mainline f612925f989).
+ */
+static void cdns_i2c_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct cdns_i2c *id = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+
+	if (!id)
+		return;
+
+	/* Mark the adapter as suspended to prevent further I2C transfers */
+	i2c_mark_adapter_suspended(&id->adap);
+
+	/* Reset the controller state if active - clocks are off when suspended */
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pdev->dev))
+		cdns_i2c_master_reset(&id->adap);
+}
+
 static struct platform_driver cdns_i2c_drv = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name  = DRIVER_NAME,
@@ -1632,6 +1654,7 @@ static struct platform_driver cdns_i2c_drv = {
 	},
 	.probe  = cdns_i2c_probe,
 	.remove_new = cdns_i2c_remove,
+	.shutdown = cdns_i2c_shutdown,
 };
 
 module_platform_driver(cdns_i2c_drv);
